      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: persistence prior = latest same-series BLS/FRED value, 1.9; this is the time-series model prior, with no separate fitted model. Historical sample = contiguous monthly SA Total quits rates Jan-May 2026: 2.0, 1.9, 2.0, 1.9, 1.9. Adjustment components: level 0.00 from latest 1.9, momentum 0.00 from Apr-to-May change 0.0, openings/hires mix +0.02 because openings rate is firm at 4.6 while hires is flat at 3.3, rounded back to the one-decimal first-print center of 1.9. For interval, successive monthly changes are -0.1, +0.1, -0.1, 0.0; one-month sample sigma = 0.10, so May-to-July two-month horizon sigma = 0.10*sqrt(2) = 0.14, and 80% half-width = 1.28*0.14 = 0.18. Final implied bounds: 1.90 - 0.18 = 1.72 and 1.90 + 0.18 = 2.08."
